----------
module local/test/main
----------

// Error test: a return that some path reaches without writing the out param.
//
// Writing it in one branch and not the other is not itself the error, and
// reporting there refused a function that writes after the branch instead.
// What is wrong here is the `ret`, which the `cond == false` path arrives at
// with `x` unwritten, and that is the one report.
fun bad_function(out x: u32, cond: bool): bool
    if cond
        set x = 42
    end if
    ret true
end fun

----------
scriptunit-fragment
----------

require module local/test/main
import main.bad_function

